<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_1" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn">
  <bpmn:process id="Process_ItemStockPlacement" name="Item Stock Placement (per-item)" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>
      Workflow 050: Item Stock Convergence — One Workflow Per Item.

      Triggered by either of two signals from pyck inventory service:

        inventory.item.create   - item just landed (first-time seed)
        inventory.item.update   - any item mutation (master-data sync
                                  from upstream WMS, or operator edit)

      The pyck signal router extracts the entity ID from the event
      payload and sets it as the workflow ID suffix (pyck_data_id).
      Workflow ID is therefore deterministic per item:

        ACME_Stock_ItemStockPlacement_&lt;item-uuid&gt;

      Re-signalling the same item terminates any in-flight execution
      and starts a new one (WORKFLOW_ID_CONFLICT_POLICY_TERMINATE_EXISTING).
      This is safe because PlaceItemStock is a delta converger that
      reads canonical pyck state on every call and recomputes from
      scratch — partial work left by a terminated run is detected and
      either re-used (orphan with matching qty) or cleanly replaced
      (orphan with stale qty: delete + recreate).

      Invariant:

        After a successful run, the picking slot's ownQuantity equals
        targetStock (the WMS-supplied target). Total physical stock
        per item never exceeds what the upstream WMS sent. Mid-pick
        drift (executed reservations) takes ownQty BELOW target; the
        next WMS update re-converges.

      Flow:

        Start -&gt; Place Item Stock -&gt; End

      The single service task is a delta converger. It reads the
      target (item.data.targetStock), the current physical state
      at the Z2 slot (ownQuantity from pyck's append-only stock
      table), and the pending picker reservations (executed=false
      outbound ItemMovements). It computes a signed delta and emits
      ONE of three outcomes:

        SEED   (delta &gt; 0): VIRTUAL-INBOUND      -&gt; slot
        DRAIN  (delta &lt; 0): slot                 -&gt; WRITE-OFF-MASTERDATA
        NOOP   (delta == 0): no movement; only stockPlaced bookkeeping

      DRAIN is the loud direction — it physically removes units the
      warehouse used to have, in response to the upstream WMS lowering
      targetStock. If pending picker reservations would be stranded
      by the drain (target &lt; outgoingStock), the converger proceeds
      anyway per the operator-decided invariant. WF102's existing
      shortage logic (write-off + redistribute + partial-pick) handles
      the picker disruption.

      No user tasks. No gateways. No loops. Skipped outcomes (no
      targetStock, no Z2 storage slot) complete successfully
      without converging — they are not errors.

      Race notes (see activity godoc for the full matrix):

      - Reservations landing between the slot-state read and the
        movement create do not duplicate stock. SEED is safe regardless
        (inbound does not validate against outgoingStock). DRAIN may
        be rejected by pyck if a fresh reservation pushes outgoing
        above the post-drain ownQty; Temporal retries with a fresh,
        smaller delta.
      - Worker crashes between executeMovement and markItemPlaced
        leave stockPlaced stale but ownQty correct. On retry, the
        delta from ownQty is zero and the converger short-circuits
        to NOOP — no duplicate movement.
      - Concurrent triggers for the same item are serialised by
        TERMINATE_EXISTING. A stale orphan from the killed run is
        detected (handler + fromID + executed=false query) and
        either reused (matching qty) or deleted+recreated (mismatch).
    </bpmn:documentation>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_1" name="Item created or updated&#10;(inventory.item.create OR inventory.item.update)">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_StartToPlace</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:signalEventDefinition id="SignalDef_1" />
    </bpmn:startEvent>

    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Activity_PlaceItemStock" name="Place Item Stock">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        Single atomic activity. Steps internally:
          1. Fetch item by id, read targetStock (target qty).
          2. Skip if no targetStock or no Z2 storage slot.
          3. Resolve three repo IDs: target slot, VIRTUAL-INBOUND,
             WRITE-OFF-MASTERDATA. (Both source/sink up front so a
             missing virtual repo is a hard config error caught early.)
          4. Read current ownQty at slot (latest stock row).
          5. Read pending outgoing reservations at slot (sum of
             executed=false outbound ItemMovements).
          6. delta = targetStock - ownQty.
             delta &gt; 0  -&gt; SEED  movement  (VIRTUAL-INBOUND      -&gt; slot)
             delta &lt; 0  -&gt; DRAIN movement  (slot                 -&gt; WRITE-OFF-MASTERDATA)
             delta == 0 -&gt; NOOP (write stockPlaced bookkeeping only)
          7. find-or-create the movement, handler-scoped orphan
             recovery: reuse matching orphan, delete + recreate on
             qty mismatch, fresh create when no orphan exists.
          8. Execute movement.
          9. Update item.data.stockPlaced / stockPlacedAt /
             stockPlacementRepo to targetStock.

        On DRAIN with stranded reservations (target &lt; outgoingStock),
        the activity logs a WARN and proceeds anyway. Pickers will
        hit shortage errors at scan time; WF102 shortage logic copes.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_StartToPlace</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_PlaceToEnd</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_1" name="Done">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_PlaceToEnd</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_StartToPlace" sourceRef="StartEvent_1" targetRef="Activity_PlaceItemStock" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_PlaceToEnd" sourceRef="Activity_PlaceItemStock" targetRef="EndEvent_1" />
  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="Process_ItemStockPlacement">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_1_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_1">
        <dc:Bounds x="91" y="72" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="50" y="115" width="119" height="75" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Activity_PlaceItemStock_di" bpmnElement="Activity_PlaceItemStock">
        <dc:Bounds x="379" y="50" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_1_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_1">
        <dc:Bounds x="571" y="72" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <dc:Bounds x="575" y="115" width="29" height="15" />
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_StartToPlace_di" bpmnElement="Flow_StartToPlace">
        <di:waypoint x="127" y="90" />
        <di:waypoint x="379" y="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_PlaceToEnd_di" bpmnElement="Flow_PlaceToEnd">
        <di:waypoint x="479" y="90" />
        <di:waypoint x="571" y="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
